<title>FRANCE: Renault eases on Belgian court decision.</title>
<headline>Renault eases on Belgian court decision.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French car maker Renault dropped after Belgian news agency Belga said that a Belgian court had decided that the Vilvoorde plant closure was illegal.</p>
<p>Renault was 2.82 percent lower at 127.40 franc at 1312 GMT after it had been trading 1.6 percent down before the news of the court decision.</p>
</text>
